Title: "Spec Operator Alias"
Id: "bac6c9f6-1470-405d-af15-4488b254febd"

Text: "Specification capabilities use `:->` for one-way implication and `:<->:` for
equivalence. Either spelling may have multiple semicolon-separated conclusions.

```mlg-fragment
Requires:
. capability: x_ \"in\" X :-> x_ member_of X

Requires:
. capability: x_ \"in\" X :-> \\abstract

Enables:
. capability: x_ \"in\" X :<->: x_ member_of X
```

The left side is a specification-like form. The right side is the specification
or builtin target established when the capability matches. Reverse inference
for `:<->:` is available only when every conclusion is established."
Id: "2e4d2b38-dfa0-42a4-8a58-bfb3d8859df2"
